WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
A FedRAMP Moderate effort depends on a clear system boundary.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:22.200
The boundary defines what cloud service offering is in scope: the application components, infrastructure, data stores, management interfaces, integrations, external services, identity systems, network paths, operational processes, and supporting tools that are part of the assessed service.

3
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.580
If the boundary is vague, every later conversation about controls and evidence becomes harder.

4
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.740
Boundary work is not just diagramming boxes.

5
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:44.840
Teams need to understand data flows, administrative access paths, tenant separation, logging paths, backup locations, support access, build and deployment systems, monitoring tools, and external dependencies.

6
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.940
A dependency may provide a critical inherited control, or it may create a responsibility gap.

7
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.680
Either way, it needs to be visible.

8
00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.340
Moderate assessment work depends on knowing where the service begins and ends.

9
00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.340
Shared responsibility should be written in plain language.

10
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:11.680
Provider-managed responsibilities might include platform hardening, vulnerability scanning, centralized logging, incident response, configuration baselines, and operational monitoring.

11
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:20.500
Customer-managed responsibilities might include user administration, tenant configuration, data handling decisions, or agency-specific procedures.

12
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.240
Some responsibilities may be shared.

13
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.740
The point is not to push responsibility away; it is to assign it accurately.

14
00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.140
Unclear boundaries create evidence gaps and risk misunderstandings.

15
00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:39.320
A provider may assume the platform handles a control while the platform assumes the application owner handles it.

16
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.900
A customer may assume a security feature is automatic when it actually requires tenant configuration.

17
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:53.440
A Moderate authorization effort is healthier when the team can trace each responsibility to an owner, an implementation, and evidence that reflects the live system.
